WEBVTT

00:00:05.460 --> 00:00:07.980
I love baseball.

00:00:08.690 --> 00:00:11.570
The reason I love baseball so much is...

00:00:11.570 --> 00:00:15.320
Essay recital

00:00:11.570 --> 00:00:15.320
"Dreams for 
the future"

00:00:12.070 --> 00:00:15.320
...because I love my father.

00:00:16.110 --> 00:00:20.830
My pop—My father is a pro baseball player.

00:00:21.280 --> 00:00:24.320
In the past, he's pitched in 
the MLB in America,

00:00:24.330 --> 00:00:28.170
and he's also played for 
the Japanese national team.

00:00:28.640 --> 00:00:30.610
But now, since he hurt his shoulder,

00:00:30.610 --> 00:00:35.090
he's giving it his all as a batter 
in the Japanese pro league.

00:00:35.090 --> 00:00:43.600
My Dream

00:00:35.800 --> 00:00:42.340
I really, really love my father
because he's always strong and cool.

00:00:43.960 --> 00:00:45.870
When I grow up,

00:00:46.550 --> 00:00:51.620
I also want to be a pro baseball 
player like my father!

00:00:52.520 --> 00:00:55.200
And I want to play in the major leagues,

00:00:56.000 --> 00:00:58.160
and become the best in the world!

00:00:58.990 --> 00:01:00.320
"My Dream"...

00:01:03.900 --> 00:01:05.320
...by Shigeno Daigo!

00:02:37.410 --> 00:02:38.550
Rock, paper...

00:02:37.510 --> 00:02:42.680
Daigo's Dream

00:02:38.550 --> 00:02:39.310
scissors!

00:02:39.720 --> 00:02:41.200
And shoot!

00:02:41.200 --> 00:02:42.540
And shoot!

00:02:42.540 --> 00:02:44.260
I won!

00:02:45.300 --> 00:02:47.460
All right, Daigo won.

00:02:47.460 --> 00:02:48.730
What do you want to watch?

00:02:48.730 --> 00:02:50.620
Pop's World Series!

00:02:50.620 --> 00:02:52.580
What? Again?

00:02:55.120 --> 00:03:00.510
<i>Pitcher: Number 56, Goro Shigeno!</i>

00:03:00.510 --> 00:03:01.490
Pop!

00:03:01.490 --> 00:03:05.060
Jeez, we already know the 
result. It was 12 years ago.

00:03:05.060 --> 00:03:07.300
The catcher is Satou Toshiya!

00:03:07.810 --> 00:03:11.000
He's been friends with Pop
since they were both little.

00:03:11.000 --> 00:03:12.340
You're right.

00:03:12.340 --> 00:03:15.360
They were huge rivals 
up until high school, though.

00:03:15.360 --> 00:03:16.920
Wow.

00:03:16.920 --> 00:03:21.010
I'll join the local team when I get to
the fourth grade, just like they did!

00:03:21.010 --> 00:03:25.510
Whoa, that means we'll be a family
full of baseball players!

00:03:25.510 --> 00:03:28.990
That's true! After all, I used to play, too.

00:03:29.380 --> 00:03:31.890
You and Pop were a battery, weren't you?

00:03:32.820 --> 00:03:33.600
Yeah, kinda.

00:03:33.960 --> 00:03:36.810
Next year, I'll join the baseball 
team at my middle school.

00:03:37.340 --> 00:03:38.230
<i>Pop...</i>

00:03:40.940 --> 00:03:44.660
<i>I wish I could play catch with Pop...</i>

00:03:47.260 --> 00:03:48.700
Ack! It's Gibson Jr.!

00:03:48.940 --> 00:03:51.470
Go! Strike him out in three!

00:03:51.470 --> 00:03:55.090
Keep it down, Sis. Haven't you
already watched this countless times?

00:03:56.670 --> 00:03:58.960
Goro

00:03:58.330 --> 00:04:01.280
Oh, it's your pop.

00:04:01.890 --> 00:04:02.970
Hello?

00:04:03.230 --> 00:04:07.120
<i>Hey, it's done. I passed the tryouts.</i>

00:04:07.120 --> 00:04:09.450
<i>I'll be playing in the Taiwanese league
from next season!</i>

00:04:09.450 --> 00:04:12.290
R-Really? Congratulations!

00:04:12.290 --> 00:04:13.230
Ah, and what else?

00:04:14.210 --> 00:04:17.230
What? You're supposed to go join 
their training camp right away?!

00:04:21.290 --> 00:04:22.700
All right, I'm off.

00:04:23.300 --> 00:04:25.060
Don't overstretch yourself, you hear?

00:04:25.060 --> 00:04:26.620
Give it everything you've got, Pop!

00:04:26.840 --> 00:04:27.660
Right on!

00:04:27.660 --> 00:04:29.650
Bring us presents when you come home.

00:04:29.650 --> 00:04:31.340
Sure! You got it!

00:04:31.340 --> 00:04:35.060
Oh, I almost forgot. This is for you, Daigo.

00:04:35.060 --> 00:04:36.460
Huh? What is it?

00:04:38.130 --> 00:04:39.420
A glove!

00:04:39.930 --> 00:04:42.420
You're joining the Dolphins in April, right?

00:04:42.420 --> 00:04:45.260
Let's race to see who 
becomes a regular first!

00:04:46.920 --> 00:04:47.590
All right!

00:04:47.850 --> 00:04:52.750
Not fair! I'm joining the baseball team 
at my middle school in April too, y'know.

00:04:52.750 --> 00:04:55.140
I gave you one before...

00:04:55.140 --> 00:04:56.840
It's in tatters now.

00:04:56.840 --> 00:04:59.140
All right, all right. Next time, okay?

00:04:59.140 --> 00:05:01.840
Pop, let's play catch!

00:05:01.840 --> 00:05:03.280
Sounds good!

00:05:03.280 --> 00:05:05.490
Your flight's leaving soon!

00:05:07.670 --> 00:05:12.750
Pop, let's play catch when you come back!

00:05:12.750 --> 00:05:14.750
Shigeno

00:05:28.010 --> 00:05:34.020
Shigeno Goro makes the starting 
lineup in the Taiwanese league

00:05:35.050 --> 00:05:37.430
Daigo, here's your towel.

00:05:37.430 --> 00:05:38.480
Ah, right.

00:05:38.480 --> 00:05:41.050
Have you got everything? Your glove?

00:05:41.050 --> 00:05:42.180
It's in there.

00:05:42.180 --> 00:05:45.080
Make sure to greet the manager 
and the coach properly.

00:05:45.080 --> 00:05:47.610
They're your pop's old baseball buddies.

00:05:48.020 --> 00:05:50.200
I will. I'm off!

00:06:04.020 --> 00:06:06.160
<i>So this is the Mifune Dolphins.</i>

00:06:07.330 --> 00:06:10.260
<i>Today is my first step toward </i>real<i> baseball.</i>

00:06:10.730 --> 00:06:12.260
Gather round!

00:06:13.150 --> 00:06:18.320
Let's introduce the new fourth graders who
are joining the Mifune Dolphins this year.

00:06:18.680 --> 00:06:20.800
State your school and your name.

00:06:20.800 --> 00:06:22.270
Takami Grade School: Kimura!

00:06:22.800 --> 00:06:24.820
Takami Grade School: Ariyoshi!

00:06:24.820 --> 00:06:26.660
Takami Grade School: Kishimoto!

00:06:26.660 --> 00:06:28.140
Yamamuro Grade School...

00:06:27.270 --> 00:06:29.080
Hey, speak up!

00:06:29.080 --> 00:06:29.910
Sorry.

00:06:30.200 --> 00:06:32.410
Yamamuro Grade School: Matsubara!

00:06:32.410 --> 00:06:34.030
Yamamuro Grade School: Nagai!

00:06:34.030 --> 00:06:36.040
Yamamuro Grade School: Katsumoto!

00:06:36.330 --> 00:06:37.640
All right! And last in line...

00:06:37.640 --> 00:06:38.480
Yessir!

00:06:39.870 --> 00:06:41.880
Mifune Grade School: Shigeno!

00:06:42.200 --> 00:06:43.550
Huh? "Shigeno"?

00:06:43.550 --> 00:06:45.420
"Shigeno"? Could he be...

00:06:45.760 --> 00:06:48.020
Yes, that's right. Shigeno Daigo.

00:06:48.020 --> 00:06:51.100
He's the brother of Shigeno Izumi 
who was with us up until last year.

00:06:51.100 --> 00:06:53.890
Which means that he's 
the son of Shigeno Goro.

00:06:53.890 --> 00:06:55.430
Oh, Izumi-san's brother...

00:06:55.640 --> 00:06:57.320
Shigeno the Second, huh?

00:06:57.320 --> 00:06:59.470
We've got a super rookie on our hands.

00:07:00.350 --> 00:07:03.270
<i>Pop really </i>is<i> a superstar.</i>

00:07:03.660 --> 00:07:10.500
As you're aware, Shigeno Goro started in
Little League and made it to the top.

00:07:10.500 --> 00:07:11.870
So follow his example, everyone!

00:07:11.870 --> 00:07:13.280
Yes, sir!

00:07:13.280 --> 00:07:14.860
All right, let's begin practice!

00:07:14.860 --> 00:07:15.920
Yes, sir!

00:07:16.780 --> 00:07:18.930
His dad went to the major leagues, you know.

00:07:18.930 --> 00:07:21.310
He was supposed to be 
really good as a kid, too.

00:07:21.310 --> 00:07:24.500
I bet his son's amazing, too.

00:07:28.270 --> 00:07:30.010
All right. Newcomers up next!

00:07:30.230 --> 00:07:31.660
We'll go in order.

00:07:31.660 --> 00:07:32.470
Yes, sir!

00:07:35.900 --> 00:07:36.310
Next!

00:07:44.690 --> 00:07:46.000
I'm sorry.

00:07:46.450 --> 00:07:47.600
Next. Daigo!

00:07:47.600 --> 00:07:48.440
Yessir!

00:07:50.740 --> 00:07:53.710
<i>We've always been together.</i>

00:07:54.550 --> 00:07:56.580
<i>Ever since I was born, 
I've always had baseball.</i>

00:07:58.210 --> 00:07:59.180
<i>That's why...</i>

00:08:02.340 --> 00:08:03.980
<i>I don't want to lose to anyone!</i>

00:08:20.610 --> 00:08:22.940
Huh? It bounced again.

00:08:22.940 --> 00:08:25.020
Isn't that pretty average 
for a fourth grader?

00:08:26.750 --> 00:08:27.780
Last one!

00:08:34.520 --> 00:08:36.110
I-I'm sorry!

00:08:37.570 --> 00:08:38.900
What's he doing?

00:08:54.930 --> 00:08:56.130
<i>Dammit...</i>

00:08:56.930 --> 00:08:59.280
<i>I'll show them next time!</i>

00:09:03.700 --> 00:09:06.320
We're going to assess which positions 
you have an affinity for.

00:09:06.860 --> 00:09:09.110
Does anyone have a preference?

00:09:10.570 --> 00:09:13.280
Yes! I'd like to be a pitcher!

00:09:13.540 --> 00:09:17.900
Daigo? Well, I guess both your 
dad and sister were pitchers.

00:09:18.410 --> 00:09:19.620
All right. Give it a try.

00:09:20.140 --> 00:09:20.950
Yes, sir!

00:09:25.210 --> 00:09:26.870
All right, show me what you got.

00:09:27.210 --> 00:09:29.100
<i>I've practiced my pitching a lot.</i>

00:09:29.760 --> 00:09:30.960
<i>Especially my control.</i>

00:09:46.870 --> 00:09:48.620
All right, that'll do.

00:09:49.330 --> 00:09:52.630
All your pitches were strikes. 
Your control is great.

00:09:53.980 --> 00:09:57.990
However, Daigo... it's too soon for 
you to be pitching, I'm afraid.

00:09:58.280 --> 00:09:59.160
Huh?

00:10:00.020 --> 00:10:03.730
I noticed it when you were throwing 
during the defense drill, too.

00:10:03.730 --> 00:10:05.750
Right now, your shoulder isn't very strong.

00:10:06.520 --> 00:10:08.470
Even compared to other kids your age.

00:10:10.080 --> 00:10:13.950
I understand why you want to do it, 
but for now, don't insist on pitching.

00:10:13.950 --> 00:10:16.110
Work on building up your muscles instead.

00:10:16.110 --> 00:10:18.550
You'll still have time to
become a pitcher after that.

00:10:18.780 --> 00:10:20.040
B-But...

00:10:22.250 --> 00:10:23.640
U-Um...

00:10:24.200 --> 00:10:29.800
I've always played pitcher at school, so if possible, I'd like to try that...

00:10:29.800 --> 00:10:32.200
Really? All right, try pitching some.

00:10:32.200 --> 00:10:33.020
Yes, sir!

00:10:34.630 --> 00:10:36.470
Not bad at all.

00:10:36.910 --> 00:10:39.120
Try throwing it without 
tensing up. Just relax.

00:10:39.600 --> 00:10:40.490
Yes, sir!

00:10:43.220 --> 00:10:44.340
Nice one.

00:10:51.360 --> 00:10:53.640
All right, Kimura. Nice swing.

00:10:53.640 --> 00:10:54.460
Thank you.

00:10:55.420 --> 00:10:56.980
Thank you very much!

00:10:58.950 --> 00:11:00.470
Let's do this.

00:11:01.680 --> 00:11:04.470
I hear Shigeno the Second didn't make pitcher.

00:11:04.470 --> 00:11:07.560
Really? Even though he's Shigeno Goro's son?

00:11:09.640 --> 00:11:10.940
Strike!

00:11:11.200 --> 00:11:13.480
Hey, Daigo! Keep your eyes on the ball!

00:11:13.770 --> 00:11:16.540
Being his son doesn't 
automatically make him good.

00:11:16.540 --> 00:11:19.030
Izumi-san was amazing, though.

00:11:25.490 --> 00:11:27.750
Thank you very much!

00:11:48.430 --> 00:11:50.180
Shigeno

00:12:04.830 --> 00:12:07.260
<i>Izumi-san was amazing, though.</i>

00:12:12.010 --> 00:12:13.520
Oh, Daigo?

00:12:13.520 --> 00:12:14.490
Welcome home.

00:12:16.180 --> 00:12:17.230
What's wrong?

00:12:17.700 --> 00:12:18.750
I'm going out again.

00:12:18.750 --> 00:12:19.710
Going where?

00:12:20.020 --> 00:12:21.240
Practice!

00:12:22.600 --> 00:12:23.820
Daigo...

00:12:28.900 --> 00:12:29.970
<i>Practice!</i>

00:12:31.940 --> 00:12:34.690
<i>If I practice, then I'm sure I'll...</i>

00:12:50.240 --> 00:12:54.250
<i>If I work hard, I'm sure I can 
become as good as Pop!</i>

00:12:55.670 --> 00:12:56.250
<i>I know I can!</i>

00:13:10.390 --> 00:13:11.260
<i>Pop...</i>

00:13:11.770 --> 00:13:14.680
Let's race to see who 
becomes a regular first!

00:13:21.950 --> 00:13:23.210
I've got it!

00:13:23.980 --> 00:13:25.390
Nice one, right fielder!

00:13:25.390 --> 00:13:26.740
One out! One out!

00:13:26.920 --> 00:13:28.570
Defense! Defense!

00:13:31.030 --> 00:13:33.030
I hope Daigo gets to play.

00:13:33.030 --> 00:13:34.040
Me, too.

00:13:34.040 --> 00:13:35.910
Team

00:13:34.040 --> 00:13:35.910
Mifune

00:13:34.040 --> 00:13:35.910
Yamate

00:13:40.170 --> 00:13:41.590
You can do it! You can do it!

00:13:41.590 --> 00:13:42.790
Hit the ball! Hit the ball!

00:13:42.790 --> 00:13:44.520
Turn it around!

00:13:44.520 --> 00:13:47.870
Right. We're going to use a fourth 
grader to pinch hit for us!

00:13:48.280 --> 00:13:49.470
Kimura, go!

00:13:49.470 --> 00:13:50.240
Yes, sir!

00:13:52.830 --> 00:13:55.090
Strike! Batter out!

00:13:56.200 --> 00:13:57.350
Another one!

00:13:57.800 --> 00:13:59.440
Daigo, go!

00:14:00.990 --> 00:14:01.820
Yes, sir!

00:14:01.820 --> 00:14:03.860
Daigo, you can do this!

00:14:04.900 --> 00:14:05.910
<i>This is my chance.</i>

00:14:06.460 --> 00:14:07.650
<i>I'll hit this one</i>

00:14:08.120 --> 00:14:09.740
<i>and make myself a regular!</i>

00:14:10.870 --> 00:14:15.870
<i>Pop, I'll show them what 
Shigeno Goro the Second is made of!</i>

00:14:19.380 --> 00:14:20.420
Strike!

00:14:25.260 --> 00:14:26.210
Foul!

00:14:28.030 --> 00:14:29.970
<i>I practiced every day.</i>

00:14:30.440 --> 00:14:31.970
<i>I </i>will<i> hit it!</i>

00:14:41.590 --> 00:14:44.280
Strike! Batter out!

00:14:44.280 --> 00:14:45.600
And that's game.

00:14:55.150 --> 00:14:57.170
I'm sorry, Pop.

00:14:58.120 --> 00:15:00.560
It looks like I'm mediocre at best.

00:15:01.540 --> 00:15:05.230
I can never be like you.

00:15:16.060 --> 00:15:18.560
2 years later

00:15:30.950 --> 00:15:33.200
Okay! Next, outfield!

00:15:34.410 --> 00:15:35.560
Got it!

00:15:36.540 --> 00:15:37.610
Okay!

00:15:50.880 --> 00:15:52.720
Hey, Tashiro!

00:15:52.940 --> 00:15:54.840
Isn't this thing <i>amazing?</i>

00:15:55.140 --> 00:15:57.490
Fujii! What <i>is</i> that thing?

00:15:57.490 --> 00:15:59.060
Wow.

00:15:59.910 --> 00:16:04.220
I know I asked you to be coach, 
but I didn't tell you to buy a bus!

00:16:05.230 --> 00:16:08.270
Impressive, isn't it? It's our team bus.

00:16:08.560 --> 00:16:10.750
It's got "Dolphins" written on it here.

00:16:10.750 --> 00:16:11.820
Wow.

00:16:12.060 --> 00:16:14.880
Hey! The team doesn't have
the money for this!

00:16:14.880 --> 00:16:18.570
Don't worry. I wasn't the one who bought it.

00:16:18.570 --> 00:16:19.410
Huh?

00:16:20.880 --> 00:16:22.000
Hello.

00:16:22.980 --> 00:16:23.950
Who's that?

00:16:23.950 --> 00:16:25.780
I recognize her from somewhere...

00:16:26.330 --> 00:16:28.290
Oh, it's Shigeno's mother!

00:16:28.470 --> 00:16:30.030
It's Daigo's mother!

00:16:30.030 --> 00:16:32.510
Oh, right. He used to be on 
the team back in fourth grade.

00:16:32.510 --> 00:16:35.560
Great! Now we can play many more away games!

00:16:35.560 --> 00:16:36.890
Yeah!

00:16:36.890 --> 00:16:38.470
Let's all thank her!

00:16:38.470 --> 00:16:39.670
All together now!

00:16:39.670 --> 00:16:42.250
Thank you very much!

00:16:43.800 --> 00:16:45.310
Hey, catch it in front! In front!

00:16:46.020 --> 00:16:47.820
Okay, nice.

00:16:47.820 --> 00:16:48.970
All right. Next.

00:16:52.390 --> 00:16:54.760
Seriously, thank you, Kaoru-chan.

00:16:54.760 --> 00:16:56.530
But are you sure about this?

00:16:56.530 --> 00:16:57.960
It's fine, really!

00:16:57.960 --> 00:16:59.370
Don't worry about it.

00:16:59.370 --> 00:17:03.860
My husband's been saying 
he's wanted to do this since forever.

00:17:05.130 --> 00:17:09.750
And since he plays in Taiwan,
he barely gets to spend any time in Japan.

00:17:10.100 --> 00:17:14.830
So he at least wants to help out
the baseball-mad kids in the area this way.

00:17:16.660 --> 00:17:19.470
That way, he can find the strength
to keep fighting.

00:17:21.060 --> 00:17:22.090
Ah, I see.

00:17:23.000 --> 00:17:26.860
While he's at it, there's a baseball-mad
old dude who could do with an import—

00:17:26.860 --> 00:17:28.060
No chance.

00:17:29.230 --> 00:17:33.400
Anyway, how long is that baseball 
fanatic going to keep on playing?

00:17:34.170 --> 00:17:36.910
I have no idea, either.

00:17:37.490 --> 00:17:40.350
And given he's such a baseball fanatic,

00:17:40.890 --> 00:17:45.320
why did his son quit the sport within a year?

00:17:46.470 --> 00:17:47.640
Daigo, huh?

00:17:48.620 --> 00:17:52.390
He joined a soccer team 
after he quit the Dolphins, right?

00:17:52.670 --> 00:17:54.380
He quit that, too.

00:17:54.380 --> 00:17:55.300
Huh?

00:17:56.540 --> 00:17:59.260
Seems like nothing sticks.

00:18:00.260 --> 00:18:04.270
Maybe sports just aren't his bag.

00:18:08.610 --> 00:18:10.260
I'm home.

00:18:39.280 --> 00:18:42.940
Daigo, don't you have better things to do?

00:18:45.080 --> 00:18:48.060
You want to go to Fuurin Middle
like me, don't you?

00:18:48.060 --> 00:18:49.810
You won't get in playing games!

00:18:50.140 --> 00:18:51.150
I don't care.

00:18:53.180 --> 00:18:55.460
I have no intention of 
going to a private school.

00:18:56.060 --> 00:18:57.860
Are you serious?

00:18:57.860 --> 00:19:03.740
You promised Mom you'd study hard and
try to get into Fuurin if you quit soccer!

00:19:03.740 --> 00:19:07.000
Yeah. I said I'd try, not that I'd get in.

00:19:11.360 --> 00:19:13.990
What are you doing?! I hadn't saved yet!

00:19:13.990 --> 00:19:16.340
I've had it with your crap!

00:19:16.980 --> 00:19:19.090
What will it take for you to get serious?!

00:19:19.520 --> 00:19:20.770
You gave up on baseball.

00:19:20.770 --> 00:19:22.110
You gave up on soccer.

00:19:22.110 --> 00:19:25.390
I figured you'd at least study,
but you don't want to do that, either!

00:19:25.840 --> 00:19:29.890
I don't particularly care what kind of
life my brother ends up leading,

00:19:29.890 --> 00:19:33.820
but shouldn't you try to live up to
our parents' expectations for once?!

00:19:42.720 --> 00:19:45.330
Must be so nice to be you, Sis...

00:19:47.400 --> 00:19:49.480
You don't understand what it's like!

00:19:49.480 --> 00:19:51.800
You're good at baseball, 
and you've got good grades.

00:19:52.320 --> 00:19:55.600
All your life, you've easily
met their expectations.

00:19:56.630 --> 00:19:58.960
What could you possibly
 understand about me?!

00:20:00.900 --> 00:20:02.470
Wow. I'm amazing.

00:20:02.470 --> 00:20:03.840
That's how you interpret it?!

00:20:04.350 --> 00:20:07.870
Fine. Keep being emo like that forever.

00:20:07.870 --> 00:20:08.810
This is too dumb for me.

00:20:16.520 --> 00:20:17.810
That stupid cow.

00:20:21.680 --> 00:20:23.280
<i>Dammit...</i>

00:20:25.160 --> 00:20:27.090
<i>In reality, I'd like to...</i>

00:20:32.130 --> 00:20:34.280
Hey, Mutsuko...

00:20:34.280 --> 00:20:36.210
Yeah, I heard.

00:20:36.670 --> 00:20:40.090
They've replaced tomorrow's pudding
with mozuku seaweed, right?

00:20:40.090 --> 00:20:42.030
No, not <i>that.</i>

00:20:42.030 --> 00:20:45.640
Apparently, the transfer student
who's joined Class 4 is a real hunk.

00:20:47.120 --> 00:20:51.960
He's tall, he used to live abroad, 
and he's fluent in English!

00:20:51.960 --> 00:20:54.560
That kind of thing 
doesn't really interest me.

00:20:56.560 --> 00:20:57.910
Hey! Shigeno-kun!

00:20:57.910 --> 00:21:01.320
Where do you think you're going? 
You're on cleaning duty, too!

00:21:01.820 --> 00:21:03.320
Oh, really?

00:21:03.580 --> 00:21:05.240
Don't play dumb with me.

00:21:05.240 --> 00:21:06.950
Now, go get a dustpan.

00:21:06.950 --> 00:21:08.930
Quit being a nag.

00:21:08.930 --> 00:21:11.110
Maybe if you stop trying to ditch.

00:21:11.110 --> 00:21:13.580
Excuse me, guys and gals...

00:21:16.310 --> 00:21:20.710
I'm Satou Hikaru from Class 4.

00:21:20.980 --> 00:21:23.800
Th-That's him! That's the guy!
 The transfer student!

00:21:24.140 --> 00:21:29.300
Is the son of Shigeno Goro,
the pro baseball player, in your class?

00:21:30.790 --> 00:21:34.110
This would be him right here.

00:21:34.110 --> 00:21:36.660
This is Shigeno Jr. AKA Daigo.

00:21:36.660 --> 00:21:37.560
Riko...

00:21:38.000 --> 00:21:41.440
Oh? You're Daigo-kun?

00:21:41.840 --> 00:21:43.110
Nice to meet y—

00:21:47.120 --> 00:21:50.560
Sorry, but I don't take requests
for autographs and stuff.

00:21:50.560 --> 00:21:52.950
Dad's not around, anyway.
He's in Taiwan.

00:21:53.150 --> 00:21:53.900
Huh?

00:21:54.660 --> 00:21:58.050
Oh, man, you sure jumped to conclusions.

00:21:59.150 --> 00:22:03.160
I didn't want your dad's autograph.

00:22:03.160 --> 00:22:06.340
My papa's more famous, anyway.

00:22:06.830 --> 00:22:07.840
What?!

00:22:08.200 --> 00:22:09.180
"Papa"?

00:22:10.030 --> 00:22:13.270
My papa has led the majors
 in homeruns before,

00:22:13.270 --> 00:22:15.120
and he retired last year.

00:22:15.120 --> 00:22:18.270
I'm sure you've heard of him. Satou Toshiya.

00:22:21.510 --> 00:22:27.070
<i>Th-The son of Satou Toshiya,
the man Pop won the World Series with?</i>

00:24:01.050 --> 00:24:03.580
Satou Toshiya's son?

00:24:03.790 --> 00:24:07.800
He's a "second" like me, 
but I bet he's good at baseball.

00:24:08.750 --> 00:24:10.130
Just leave me alone!

00:24:10.600 --> 00:24:13.430
I will never play baseball!

00:24:14.180 --> 00:24:15.660
I will never play in a game!

00:24:15.660 --> 00:24:17.150
Never, ever!

00:24:18.010 --> 00:24:25.020
If I Wasn't the Second

00:24:18.160 --> 00:24:20.490
Next time: "If I Wasn't the Second."

00:24:20.960 --> 00:24:23.000
Run to the stage of your dreams!
